<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Monocular depth estimation ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that the multivariate Gaussian parameterization <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}^{\mathrm{mv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>mv</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}^{\mathrm{mv}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves the best overall performance, consistently improving upon the deterministic Marigold baseline <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\delta}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\delta}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> across nearly all datasets and metrics.
Figure <a href="#S4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 4.3 Monocular depth estimation ‣ 4 Numerical experiments ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates the improvement in prediction quality and uncertainty estimation over <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\delta}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\delta}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additional experiments, metrics, and further experiment details are reported in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure">
