</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">URL <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.11650" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.11650</a>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib65" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zwicker (2020)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
David Zwicker.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">py-pde: A Python package for solving partial differential equations.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib65.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Journal of Open Source Software</em>, 5(48):2158, April 2020.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">ISSN 2475-9066.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">doi: <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_Url ltx_ref_self">10.21105/joss.02158</span>.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Approximations of the noise distribution</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Approximations of the covariance matrix</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As already mentioned, apart from only modeling the diagonal, we consider two efficient ways of parameterizing the full covariance matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cholesky decomposition</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we represent <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\theta,k}=L_{\theta,k}L_{\theta,k}^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\theta,k}=L_{\theta,k}L_{\theta,k}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math> is a lower triangular matrix with positive diagonal. This reduces the number of predicted parameters from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D(D-1)/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D(D-1)/2</annotation></semantics></math> while ensuring symmetry. To guarantee positive definiteness, we apply a softplus transformation to the diagonal of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, normalize the strictly lower part columnwise, and add a small stability constant <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=10e-6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=10e-6</annotation></semantics></math>. In practice, we found this to be sufficient to ensure a positive definite covariance matrix. The Cholesky decomposition offers several advantages <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Muschinski et al., 2024</a>]</cite>:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling is efficient and requires only a matrix-vector product.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The determinant can be computed as <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\Sigma)=(\prod_{i=1}^{D}L_{ii})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\Sigma)=(\prod_{i=1}^{D}L_{ii})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Although computing the full inverse <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> has cost <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, inverse-vector products <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math> require only <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Nevertheless, for very high-dimensional data, these computations may still be too expensive.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Low-rank + diagonal</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a more efficient alternative, we consider the low-rank + diagonal structure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rezende et al., 2014</a>]</cite></p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\theta,k}=U_{\theta,k}U_{\theta,k}^{\top}+D_{\theta,k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\theta,k}=U_{\theta,k}U_{\theta,k}^{\top}+D_{\theta,k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rank}(U_{\theta,k})=r\ll D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rank}(U_{\theta,k})=r\ll D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta,k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is a (positive) diagonal matrix. Here, <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the diagonal <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math> are both predicted by the neural network.
Using the matrix determinant lemma, we obtain <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\Sigma)=\det(D_{\theta,k})\det(\mathbf{I}_{r}+U_{\theta,k}^{\top}D_{\theta,k}^{-1}U_{\theta,k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\Sigma)=\det(D_{\theta,k})\det(\mathbf{I}_{r}+U_{\theta,k}^{\top}D_{\theta,k}^{-1}U_{\theta,k})</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be computed in <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, inverse-vector products <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math> cost <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3}+Dr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3}+Dr)</annotation></semantics></math>, while sampling is also efficient. When <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\ll D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\ll D</annotation></semantics></math>, this parameterization is nearly as efficient as the diagonal case, though less expressive than the full Cholesky form.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Low-rank + diagonal ‣ A.1 Approximations of the covariance matrix ‣ Appendix A Approximations of the noise distribution ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes the computational complexity of common operations. The low-rank plus diagonal scales favorably when <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\ll D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\ll D</annotation></semantics></math>, while Cholesky remains more costly. Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Low-rank + diagonal ‣ A.1 Approximations of the covariance matrix ‣ Appendix A Approximations of the noise distribution ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> illustrates the different correlation structures for each method during different diffusion timesteps for a selected sample of the Kuramoto–Sivashinsky equation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Computational complexity for common operations on covariance matrices <math id="A1.T4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> under different factorizations.
<math id="A1.T4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the data dimension, <math id="A1.T4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the rank of <math id="A1.T4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> in the low-rank<math id="A1.T4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>diagonal case.</figcaption>
<table id="A1.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><span id="A1.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sampling from <math id="A1.T4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0,\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\Sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\Sigma)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;">Cholesky</td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;">Low-rank <math id="A1.T4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> diag</td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Dr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Dr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2}r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2}r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(Dr^{2}+r^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;">Diagonal</td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T4.2.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b" style="padding-top:-0.75pt;padding-bottom:-0.75pt;"><math id="A1.T4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D)</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04583v1/KS_correlation_example.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/288;" width="476" height="288" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Correlation matrices for different covariance parameterizations across several time steps <math id="A1.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> for a selected sample of the Kuramoto–Sivashinsky equation.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Closed-form expressions for scoring rules</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide closed-form expressions for different scoring rules for the different instantiations of our proposed predictive distribution.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Univariate Gaussians</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For univariate Gaussians, the energy score reduces to the continuous ranked probability score (CRPS), which admits a closed-form expression <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gneiting and Raftery, 2007</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRPS}(\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2}),y)=\sigma\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\left(\Phi\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-1\right)+2\varphi\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>CRPS</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>π</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRPS}(\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2}),y)=\sigma\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\left(\Phi\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-1\right)+2\varphi\left(\frac{y-\mu}{\sigma}\right)-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\pi}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> denote the CDF and PDF of a standard normal distribution, respectively. For a Gaussian kernel with bandwidth <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding kernel score admits a closed-form solution as</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\mu.\sigma^{2}),y)=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+2\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}\exp\left(-\frac{(y-\mu)^{2}}{\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}}\right)+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{1+4\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}+\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\mu.\sigma^{2}),y)=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+2\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}\exp\left(-\frac{(y-\mu)^{2}}{\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}}\right)+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{1+4\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}+\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows a similar direction to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rustamov [2020]</a></cite>. By definition, the Gaussian kernel score is given as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2}),y)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,X^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]+\frac{1}{2}k(y,y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2}),y)=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,X^{\prime})]-\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]+\frac{1}{2}k(y,y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="k=\exp(-\|x-x^{\prime}\|^{2}/2\gamma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=\exp(-\|x-x^{\prime}\|^{2}/2\gamma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with the second term, which we can write as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}}e^{-(x-y)^{2}/\gamma^{2}}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{-(x-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{\mathbb{R}}e^{-(x-y)^{2}/\gamma^{2}}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{-(x-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}\int_{\mathbb{R}}(\pi\gamma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{-(x-y)^{2}/\gamma^{2}}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{(x-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></msub></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}\int_{\mathbb{R}}(\pi\gamma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{-(x-y)^{2}/\gamma^{2}}(2\pi\sigma^{2})^{-1/2}e^{(x-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2})}\,dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x-y)^{2}=(y-x)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x-y)^{2}=(y-x)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, this can be expressed as the convolution of two densities</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}(f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}\ast f_{0,\gamma^{2}/2})(y)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}(f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}\ast f_{0,\gamma^{2}/2})(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the pdf of a Gaussian. By the convolution theorem of Gaussian random variables, we know that <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}\ast f_{0,\gamma^{2}/2})(y)=f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}+\gamma^{2}/2}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}}\ast f_{0,\gamma^{2}/2})(y)=f_{\mu,\sigma^{2}+\gamma^{2}/2}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{N}(\mu,\sigma^{2})}[k(X,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}(\pi(\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}))^{-1/2}e^{-(y-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2}+\gamma^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\pi\gamma^{2})^{1/2}(\pi(\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}))^{-1/2}e^{-(y-\mu)^{2}/(2\sigma^{2}+\gamma^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+2\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}\exp\left(-\frac{(y-\mu)^{2}}{\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+2\sigma^{2}/\gamma^{2}}}\exp\left(-\frac{(y-\mu)^{2}}{\gamma^{2}+2\sigma^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The first term can be obtained by recognizing <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X-X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,2\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X-X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,2\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and following the same steps as above.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Univariate Gaussian mixture</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{K}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\mathcal{N}(x;\mu_{i},\sigma_{i}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{K}(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}\mathcal{N}(x;\mu_{i},\sigma_{i}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> denote a <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-component normal mixture distribution. Then, a closed-form expression for the CRPS is given as</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CRPS}(F_{K},y)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}A(y-\mu_{i},\sigma_{i}^{2})-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}w_{i}A(\mu_{i}-\mu_{j},\sigma_{i}^{2}+\sigma_{j}^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>CRPS</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CRPS}(F_{K},y)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}w_{i}A(y-\mu_{i},\sigma_{i}^{2})-\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i=1}^{K}\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}w_{i}A(\mu_{i}-\mu_{j},\sigma_{i}^{2}+\sigma_{j}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\mu,\sigma^{2})=\mu\left(2\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{\sigma}\right)-1\right)+2\sigma\varphi\left(\frac{\mu}{\sigma^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><mi>σ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\mu,\sigma^{2})=\mu\left(2\Phi\left(\frac{\mu}{\sigma}\right)-1\right)+2\sigma\varphi\left(\frac{\mu}{\sigma^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Grimit et al., 2006</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multivariate Gaussian</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the case of the multivariate Gaussian <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math>, the energy score does not admit an analytical expression <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Székely and Rizzo, 2005</a>]</cite>. However, the kernel score with a Gaussian kernel does admit a closed-form, given as</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma}),\bm{y})&amp;=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det\left(I+\tfrac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}(\bm{y}-\bm{\mu})^{\top}\left(I+\tfrac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)^{-1}(\bm{y}-\bm{\mu})\right)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\det\left(I+\tfrac{4}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}+\frac{1}{2},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝝁</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma}),\bm{y})&amp;=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det\left(I+\tfrac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}(\bm{y}-\bm{\mu})^{\top}\left(I+\tfrac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)^{-1}(\bm{y}-\bm{\mu})\right)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\det\left(I+\tfrac{4}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}+\frac{1}{2},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is the bandwidth of the kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneq X-\bm{y}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z}\coloneq\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneq X-\bm{y}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z}\coloneq\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|Z\|^{2}=Z^{\top}Z=Z^{\top}AZ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|Z\|^{2}=Z^{\top}Z=Z^{\top}AZ</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=\bm{I}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=\bm{I}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a generalized chi-squared distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Das and Geisler, 2024</a>]</cite>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\top}AZ\sim\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\bm{\Sigma}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\top}AZ\sim\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\bm{\Sigma}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can express the kernel score in terms of the corresponding moment-generating function, via</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,\bm{y})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,\bm{y})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}_{Z}}\left[\exp\left(-\frac{Z^{\top}Z}{\gamma^{2}}\right)\right]=M_{\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})}\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>Z</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbb{P}_{Z}}\left[\exp\left(-\frac{Z^{\top}Z}{\gamma^{2}}\right)\right]=M_{\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})}\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the case of the generalized chi-squared distribution, the moment-generating function is given as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle M_{\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})}\left(t\right)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det(\bm{I}_{d}-2t\bm{\Sigma})}}\exp\left(t(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})^{\top}(\bm{I}_{d}-2t\bm{\Sigma})^{-1}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>χ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle M_{\tilde{\chi}(\bm{I}_{d},\bm{0},0,\bm{\mu}-\bm{y},\bm{\Sigma})}\left(t\right)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det(\bm{I}_{d}-2t\bm{\Sigma})}}\exp\left(t(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})^{\top}(\bm{I}_{d}-2t\bm{\Sigma})^{-1}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">from which we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,\bm{y})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{X\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,\bm{y})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det\left(\bm{I}_{d}+\frac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})^{\top}\left(\bm{I}_{d}+\frac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)^{-1}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mo rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\det\left(\bm{I}_{d}+\frac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)}}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{\gamma^{2}}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})^{\top}\left(\bm{I}_{d}+\frac{2}{\gamma^{2}}\bm{\Sigma}\right)^{-1}(\bm{\mu}-\bm{y})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Repeating these steps for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\coloneq X-X^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z}\coloneq\mathcal{N}(0,2\bm{\Sigma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\coloneq X-X^{\prime}\sim\mathbb{P}_{Z}\coloneq\mathcal{N}(0,2\bm{\Sigma})</annotation></semantics></math> gives the expression for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,X^{\prime})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{X,X^{\prime}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma})}[k(X,X^{\prime})]</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore the full expression for <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma}),\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{k}(\mathcal{N}(\bm{\mu},\bm{\Sigma}),\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.3 Parametrization of 𝑝_𝜃^ϵ(⋅∣𝒙_𝑡) ‣ 3 Our methodology ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start by stating a theorem concerning the distribution of a Gaussian random variable whose mean is the linear combination of another Gaussian distribution, which will serve as an important tool in many of the upcoming proofs.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{x},\Sigma_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x)=\mathcal{N}(\mu_{x},\Sigma_{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, with mean <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and positive semi-definite covariance matrix <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Further, let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with conditional distribution <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y\mid x)=\mathcal{N}(Ax+b,\Sigma_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y\mid x)=\mathcal{N}(Ax+b,\Sigma_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d},b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times d},b\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y)=\mathcal{N}(A\mu_{x}+b,A\Sigma_{x}A^{T}+\Sigma_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y)=\mathcal{N}(A\mu_{x}+b,A\Sigma_{x}A^{T}+\Sigma_{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a proof, compare Theorem 4.4.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Murphy [2014]</a></cite>, ”Machine Learning: A Probabilistic Perspective”.
We now give the proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.3 Parametrization of 𝑝_𝜃^ϵ(⋅∣𝒙_𝑡) ‣ 3 Our methodology ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we obtain an equivalent expression for (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Diffusion models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) which is now conditioned on <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{t}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(X_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}}X_{0}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{t}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(X_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}}X_{0}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mu(x_{0},x_{t})&amp;=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{x_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\\
&amp;=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\frac{x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{t}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;\eqcolon\tilde{\mu}(\epsilon_{t},x_{t})\eqcolon a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mu(x_{0},x_{t})&amp;=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}x_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{x_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}x_{0}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\\
&amp;=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\cdot\frac{x_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{t}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;\eqcolon\tilde{\mu}(\epsilon_{t},x_{t})\eqcolon a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we introduce the functions <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(x_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(x_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> for notational simplicity.
We obtain <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},\epsilon_{t})=\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}(\epsilon_{t},x_{t}),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},\epsilon_{t})=\mathcal{N}(\tilde{\mu}(\epsilon_{t},x_{t}),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}p_{\theta}^{(t)}(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t})&amp;=\int q(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},\epsilon_{t})p_{\theta}(\epsilon_{t}\mid x_{t})d\epsilon_{t}.\\
&amp;=\int\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}(\epsilon_{t};\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}))\right)d\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\int\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\mathcal{N}(\epsilon_{t};\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}))d\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+b(x_{t},t),a(x_{t},t)^{2}\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}\left(x_{t-1};\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\gamma_{t}^{2}\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}\right),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>x</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}p_{\theta}^{(t)}(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t})&amp;=\int q(x_{t-1}\mid x_{t},\epsilon_{t})p_{\theta}(\epsilon_{t}\mid x_{t})d\epsilon_{t}.\\
&amp;=\int\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\left(\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}(\epsilon_{t};\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}))\right)d\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\int\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\epsilon_{t}+b(x_{t},t),\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\mathcal{N}(\epsilon_{t};\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}))d\epsilon_{t}\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}(x_{t-1};a(x_{t},t)\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+b(x_{t},t),a(x_{t},t)^{2}\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})\\
&amp;=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\pi_{\theta}^{k}\mathcal{N}\left(x_{t-1};\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\hat{x}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mu^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t}),\gamma_{t}^{2}\Sigma^{\epsilon}_{\theta,k}(x_{t})+\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the fourth equality follows by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Approximations of the noise distribution ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and the last by plugging in the constants.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Details on CARD</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">CARD was introduced by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Han et al. [2022]</a></cite> as a framework for classification and regression tasks using diffusion.
They assume to have a pre-trained regressor <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\phi}:\mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\phi}:\mathcal{C}\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> available, which is trained on <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximates the conditional expectation <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\bm{y}\mid\bm{c}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\bm{y}\mid\bm{c}]</annotation></semantics></math> given covariates <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{c}\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒄</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{c}\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Its core idea is, that a diffusion process is used to interpolate between the noise distribution <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{y_{t}}\mid\bm{c})=\mathcal{N}(f_{\phi}(\bm{c}),\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>𝒕</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y_{t}}\mid\bm{c})=\mathcal{N}(f_{\phi}(\bm{c}),\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> and the data distribution <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{y_{0}}\mid\bm{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>𝟎</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y_{0}}\mid\bm{c})</annotation></semantics></math>.
We will provide a formulation of CARD embedded in the DDIM framework introduced earlier.
To this end, we set the mean in (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Diffusion models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) to</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(\bm{y}_{0},\bm{y}_{t})=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(\bm{c})+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{\bm{y}_{t}-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(\bm{c})\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(\bm{y}_{0},\bm{y}_{t})=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(\bm{c})+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{\bm{y}_{t}-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(\bm{c})\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which yields a modified version of (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Diffusion models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), namely</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{y}_{t}\mid\bm{y}_{0},f_{\phi}(\bm{c}))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(\bm{c}))\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{y}_{t}\mid\bm{y}_{0},f_{\phi}(\bm{c}))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\bm{y}_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(\bm{c}))\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We will prove this and the fact that we can recover the original CARD method by an appropriate choice of <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\sigma_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">The original CARD algorithm for sampling <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> given <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is specified as follows</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{cases}\hat{y}_{0}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(y_{t}-\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\theta}(x)-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}\right)\\
y_{t-1}=\gamma_{0}\hat{y}_{0}+\gamma_{1}y_{t}+\gamma_{2}f_{\phi}(x)+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z,\quad z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})\end{cases}\," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{cases}\hat{y}_{0}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(y_{t}-\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\theta}(x)-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}\right)\\
y_{t-1}=\gamma_{0}\hat{y}_{0}+\gamma_{1}y_{t}+\gamma_{2}f_{\phi}(x)+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z,\quad z\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})\end{cases}\,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{0}\coloneq\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}},\quad\gamma_{1}\coloneq\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}},\quad\gamma_{2}\coloneq\left(1+\frac{\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{0}\coloneq\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}},\quad\gamma_{1}\coloneq\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}},\quad\gamma_{2}\coloneq\left(1+\frac{\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We have</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\gamma_{0}\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(y_{t}-\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\theta}(x)-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}\right)+\gamma_{1}y_{t}+\gamma_{2}f_{\phi}(x)+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\gamma_{0}\frac{1}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\left(y_{t}-\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\theta}(x)-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}\right)+\gamma_{1}y_{t}+\gamma_{2}f_{\phi}(x)+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\frac{\gamma_{0}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\gamma_{1}\right)}_{=:A}y_{t}+\underbrace{\left(-\frac{\gamma_{0}\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\gamma_{2}\right)}_{=:B}f_{\phi}(x)-\underbrace{\frac{\gamma_{0}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}}_{=:C}\epsilon_{\theta}+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>β</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msqrt><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\left(\frac{\gamma_{0}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\gamma_{1}\right)}_{=:A}y_{t}+\underbrace{\left(-\frac{\gamma_{0}\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\gamma_{2}\right)}_{=:B}f_{\phi}(x)-\underbrace{\frac{\gamma_{0}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}}_{=:C}\epsilon_{\theta}+\sqrt{\tilde{\beta}}z</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">and calculate</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}=\frac{\beta_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}+\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\alpha_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}+\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}=\frac{\beta_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}+\frac{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)\alpha_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1-\alpha_{t}+\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1-\alpha_{t}+\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">as well as</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1+\frac{\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1+\frac{\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-(1-\alpha_{t})\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)+\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-(1-\alpha_{t})\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)+\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-1+\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\alpha_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}+\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-1+\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\alpha_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}+\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-1\right)\left(\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{-1+\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\alpha_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\alpha_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t}-\alpha_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{-1+\alpha_{t}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}-\alpha_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}+\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\alpha_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t}-\alpha_{t}-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\bar{\alpha}_{t}-1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\bar{\alpha}_{t}-1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}+1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(1-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\left(1-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.6" class="ltx_p">and lastly</p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\cdot\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta_{t}\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}{\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\cdot\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.7" class="ltx_p">In total, we obtain</p>
<table id="A2.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t-1}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t-1}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.8" class="ltx_p">To finish the argument we substitute <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A2.E15" title="In Appendix B Details on CARD ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and obtain</p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\frac{y_{t}-\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(1-\alpha_{t})}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><msqrt><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\frac{y_{t}-\left(\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(1-\alpha_{t})}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\bar{\alpha}_{t}-1+\alpha_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\bar{\alpha}_{t}-1+\alpha_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{-\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{-\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\bar{\alpha}_{t}+\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}\right)}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)^{2}}{\alpha_{t}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)+\sqrt{\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)^{2}}{\alpha_{t}\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}}\cdot\epsilon_{\theta}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}+\left(\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}+\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}+\left(\frac{\left(\alpha_{t}-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}-\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}+\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}-\sqrt{\alpha_{t}\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><msqrt><mi>α</mi></msqrt><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\sqrt{\alpha}_{t}}\left(y_{t}-\frac{1-\alpha_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\epsilon_{\theta}-\left(1-\sqrt{{\bar{\alpha}}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="A2.p2.9" class="ltx_p">We also want to show that (<a href="#A2.E16" title="In Appendix B Details on CARD ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) holds, which we will do by an induction argument, similar in style to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. [2021]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds for <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math>. We will show that it is also satisfied for <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since it is true by assumption for <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>, this would finish the proof.

<br class="ltx_break">We have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))dy_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))dy_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{y_{t}-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{y_{t}-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">corresponds to (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2.2 Diffusion models ‣ 2 Background ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>) just using the mean defined in (<a href="#A2.E15" title="In Appendix B Details on CARD ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>).
Now,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{t}\mid y_{0},f_{\phi}(x))=\mathcal{N}\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right),\left(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}\right)\mathbf{I}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">holds because of the induction hypothesis.
By theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ A.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix A Approximations of the noise distribution ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(y_{t-1}\mid y_{0},y_{t},f_{\phi}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian with mean <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance matrix <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right)-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}f_{\phi}(x)\right)-\left(\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)\right)}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}y_{0}+\left(1-\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}\right)f_{\phi}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})\mathbf{I}=(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}+\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}-\sigma_{t}^{2}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})\mathbf{I}=(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1})\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">which finishes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Experiment details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Evaluation metrics</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the true target <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}\in\mathcal{Y}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding marginals <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{k},\ k=1,\ldots,d_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{k},\ k=1,\ldots,d_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, the true predictive distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\mathcal{Y}}(\cdot\mid\bm{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mathcal{Y}}(\cdot\mid\bm{c})</annotation></semantics></math> and the learned approximate predictive distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\bm{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\bm{c})</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, define <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\bm{y}}_{i}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\bm{c}),\ i=1,\ldots,M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒄</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{y}}_{i}\sim p_{\theta}(\cdot\mid\bm{c}),\ i=1,\ldots,M</annotation></semantics></math> and the empirical predictive distribution <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}^{M}\coloneq\{\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{M}\coloneq\{\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}\}_{m=1}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. Finally, let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}\coloneq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}\coloneq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the empirical mean, <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}\coloneq\frac{1}{M-1}\sum_{m=1}^{M}(\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}-\bar{\bm{y}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}\coloneq\frac{1}{M-1}\sum_{m=1}^{M}(\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}-\bar{\bm{y}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the empirical variance of the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> marginal and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{\alpha})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{\alpha})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the empirical quantiles of the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{th}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{th}</annotation></semantics></math> marginal of <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\theta}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\theta}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> at the level <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the following evaluation metrics:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{RMSE}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>RMSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{RMSE}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\|\bar{\bm{y}}-\bm{y}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\|\bar{\bm{y}}-\bm{y}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{ES}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ES</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{ES}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\hat{\bm{y}}_{i}-\bm{y}\|_{2}-\frac{1}{2M(M-1)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}m,h=1\\
m\neq h\end{subarray}}^{M}\|\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}-\hat{\bm{y}}_{h}\|_{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\hat{\bm{y}}_{i}-\bm{y}\|_{2}-\frac{1}{2M(M-1)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}m,h=1\\
m\neq h\end{subarray}}^{M}\|\hat{\bm{y}}_{m}-\hat{\bm{y}}_{h}\|_{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{CRPS}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CRPS</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{CRPS}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E52.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left|\hat{y}_{i}^{k}-y^{k}\right|-\frac{1}{2M(M-1)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}m,h=1\\
m\neq h\end{subarray}}^{M}\left|\hat{y}_{m}^{k}-\hat{y}_{h}^{k}\right|\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>m</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>h</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\left(\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left|\hat{y}_{i}^{k}-y^{k}\right|-\frac{1}{2M(M-1)}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}m,h=1\\
m\neq h\end{subarray}}^{M}\left|\hat{y}_{m}^{k}-\hat{y}_{h}^{k}\right|\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>NLL</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{NLL}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E53.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\log\left(2\pi\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}\right)+\frac{((\bar{\bm{y}})^{k}-y^{k})^{2}}{\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\log\left(2\pi\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}\right)+\frac{((\bar{\bm{y}})^{k}-y^{k})^{2}}{\hat{\sigma}^{2}_{k}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{\alpha}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}_{\alpha}(p_{\theta}^{M},\bm{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E54.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\mathbbm{1}\left\{y^{k}\in[(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{\alpha/2})^{k},(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{1-\alpha/2})^{k}]\right\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≔</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></munderover></mstyle><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\coloneq\frac{1}{d_{y}}\sum_{k=1}^{d_{y}}\mathbbm{1}\left\{y^{k}\in[(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{\alpha/2})^{k},(\hat{q}_{\theta}^{1-\alpha/2})^{k}]\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The RMSE evaluates the match between the mean prediction <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\bm{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\bm{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the true observation, while the energy score (ES) evaluates the match for the predictive distribution as a whole. The continuous ranked probability score (CRPS) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gneiting and Raftery, 2007</a>]</cite> evaluates the predictive distribution at a pointwise level and assesses whether the predicted uncertainty fits the observations at all quantile levels for each marginal <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., whether the predictive distribution is well-calibrated. Furthermore, we analyze the negative log-likelihood (NLL) of a predictive pointwise Gaussian distribution. Although the prediction can be inherently non-Gaussian, this criterion is commonly used and describes the fit of the predictive distribution in terms of the first two estimated moments. Finally, we report the coverage <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> of the predictive distribution for selected <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-quantile levels, averaged over all marginals.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Training details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All of our proposed methods require some restricted output for the parameters, which we realize in the following way. For the marginal <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\theta,k}^{2}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\theta,k}^{2}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> we use one additional last layer with a softplus activation and add a threshold of <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> for numerical stability. For the mixture weights <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta,k}</annotation></semantics></math> we apply a softmax activation to guarantee the summation constraint. For the <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{t}^{\mathrm{ES}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ES</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{t}^{\mathrm{ES}}</annotation></semantics></math> method we concatenate the random noise as an additional channel dimension. For the multivariate normal method, implementation is already described in Section <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Approximations of the covariance matrix ‣ Appendix A Approximations of the noise distribution ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>. The remaining training details, such as batch size or number of epochs, differ across experiments and are described in the next sections, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>UCI regression</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain a fair comparison, we take the train-test splits from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hernandez-Lobato and Adams [2015]</a></cite> and do not finetune our methods on a separate validation set but use sensible hyperparameters.
We will copy the training process from the CARD method and apply it, except for some minor modifications to the number of training epochs used for our distributional methods.
In particular, we train all of our methods for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs except on the yacht dataset, where we train for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000</annotation></semantics></math>.
We only deviate from this for the larger kin8nm and protein datasets, where we train for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs, respectively.
We use the Adam optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2017</a>]</cite> with a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.001</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the diffusion process, we decided to use <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps, both during training and inference.
We use a linear noise schedule with <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.001</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{50}=0.35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>50</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{50}=0.35</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the noise schedule used to train the CARD method for <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps.
Lastly, we set <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=3</annotation></semantics></math>, when training the <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}^{\mathrm{mix}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>mix</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}^{\mathrm{mix}}</annotation></semantics></math> method and use for all of our distributional methods the CRPS score as scoring rule.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Autoregressive prediction tasks</h3>

<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Burgers’ equation</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Burgers’ equation is given as</p>
<table id="A3.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\partial_{s}u(s,x)+\partial_{x}(u^{2}(s,x)/2)&amp;=\nu/\pi\partial_{xx}u(s,x),\quad x\in(0,1),\ s\in(0,2]\\
u(0,x)&amp;=u_{0}(x),\quad x\in(0,1)\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\partial_{s}u(s,x)+\partial_{x}(u^{2}(s,x)/2)&amp;=\nu/\pi\partial_{xx}u(s,x),\quad x\in(0,1),\ s\in(0,2]\\
u(0,x)&amp;=u_{0}(x),\quad x\in(0,1)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C([0,S];H_{\mathrm{per}}^{r}((0,1);\mathbb{R}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>per</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C([0,S];H_{\mathrm{per}}^{r}((0,1);\mathbb{R}))</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\in L_{\mathrm{per}}^{2}((0,1);\mathbb{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>per</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\in L_{\mathrm{per}}^{2}((0,1);\mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial condition and <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is the diffusion coefficient<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
                
                
                
              <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{r}_{\text{per}}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R}),L^{2}_{\text{per}}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mtext>per</mtext><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>per</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{r}_{\text{per}}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R}),L^{2}_{\text{per}}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the periodic Sobolev and <math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> spaces, respectively.</span></span></span>. We utilize data from the PDEBENCH repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Takamoto et al., 2022</a>]</cite>, which assumes a constant diffusion coefficient, which we choose as <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>. The data is generated with a periodic boundary condition from a superposition of sinusoidal waves with the temporally and spatially 2nd-order upwind difference scheme for the advection term, and the central difference scheme for the diffusion term.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Kuramoto–Sivashinsky equation</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that the Kuramoto–Sivashinsky (KS-) equation in one spatial dimension is given as:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{s}u(x,s)+u\partial_{x}u(x,s)+\partial_{x}^{2}u(x,s)+\partial_{x}^{4}u(x,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{s}u(x,s)+u\partial_{x}u(x,s)+\partial_{x}^{2}u(x,s)+\partial_{x}^{4}u(x,s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0,\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x\in\mathcal{D},s\in(0,S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x\in\mathcal{D},s\in(0,S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u(x,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u(x,0)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{0}(x),\qquad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{0}(x),\qquad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle x\in\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle x\in\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\subseteq\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\subseteq\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in C([0,S];H_{\mathrm{per}}^{4}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mi>per</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in C([0,S];H_{\mathrm{per}}^{4}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R}))</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{0}\in L_{\mathrm{per}}^{2}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>per</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{0}\in L_{\mathrm{per}}^{2}(\mathcal{D};\mathbb{R})</annotation></semantics></math>. We follow the setup in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bülte et al. [2025]</a></cite> and simulate the KS-equation from random uniform noise <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}(-1,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}(-1,1)</annotation></semantics></math> on a periodic domain <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=[0,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=[0,100]</annotation></semantics></math> using the py-pde package <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zwicker, 2020</a>]</cite>. We generate 10000 samples with a resolution of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="256\times 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">256\times 50</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta s=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta s=2</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Surface temperature prediction</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the surface temperature prediction task, we utilize the ERA5 dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hersbach et al., 2020</a>]</cite> provided via the WeatherBench2 benchmark <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rasp et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. Similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bülte et al. [2025]</a></cite>, we use data with a spatial resolution of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.25^{\circ}\times 0.25^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mn>0.25</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>0.25</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.25^{\circ}\times 0.25^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> and a time resolution of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6h</annotation></semantics></math>. For computational reasons, we restrict the data to a European domain, covering an area from 35°N – 75°N and 12.5°W – 42.5°E with selected user-relevant weather variables (u-component and v-component of 10-m wind speed (U10 and V10), temperature at 2m and 850 hPa (T2M and T850), geopotential height
at 500 hPa (Z500), as well as land-sea mask and orography) that serve as input to the model. In contrast to other diffusion approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Larsson et al., 2025</a>]</cite>, we only predict the surface temperature T2M, as this is less computationally demanding. As the initial condition, we always use 00 UTC time and issue a prediction for 06 UTC time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We adapt the U-Net used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al. [2021]</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al. [2022]</a></cite> to allow for arbitrary input shapes and one-dimensional convolutions. We use 64 feature channels for the first layer and 128 channels for layers 2-4. The diffusion noise is encoded with Fourier embeddings <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Karras et al., 2022</a>]</cite>, where the noise is transformed into sine/cosine features at 32 frequencies with base period 16. Afterwards, the features are passed through a 2-layer MLP, which results in a 256-dimensional noise encoding. Finally, this encoding is added to the network through various group norms of the U-Net. The final (regular) diffusion model has 6.5 million and 15.2 million parameters for the 1D and 2D tasks, respectively. While the temperature prediction task uses a fixed prediction horizon, for the PDE tasks, we sample random timesteps <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in 1,\ldots,S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in 1,\ldots,S</annotation></semantics></math> for training and evaluation, but split the data such that the test data is unseen during training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the 1D PDE tasks, we use an effective batch size of 128, a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math> with the Adam optimizer, early stopping after 150 epochs and a learning rate scheduler that reduces the learning rate by the factor <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> if the validation loss has not improved for <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>75</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">75</annotation></semantics></math> epochs. All models are trained on an NVIDIA RTX3090 with 24GB memory.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the T2M task, we use an effective batch size of 64, a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> with the AdamW optimizer, early stopping after 300 epochs, and a learning rate scheduler that reduces the learning rate by the factor <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math> if the validation loss has not improved for <math id="A3.SS4.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150</annotation></semantics></math> epochs. All models are trained on two NVIDIA RTXA6000 with 48GB memory.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Monocular depth estimation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the setup of Marigold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ke et al., 2024</a>]</cite> in general. We only adapt the last layer of their model to our methods as described in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Training details ‣ Appendix C Experiment details ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>, the alignment of the inference ensemble, and the used metrics. Details on the Marigold setup and our adaptations are shown in the following.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Model details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The idea of Marigold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ke et al., 2024</a>]</cite> is to adapt Stable Diffusion <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022</a>]</cite> to depth estimation. The frozen VAE is used to encode the image and the corresponding depth map into the latent space for training. As the encoder expects an image with 3 channels, the depth map is replicated into three channels. The embedded RGB image is used as the conditioning <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒄</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the embedded depth map gets noise added to serve as <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. To handle this, the first layer of the UNet is duplicated, and the weights are halved to keep the scale of the activations similar. As we need multiple output channels to model the standard deviation as well, we adapt the last layer depending on the used method, as explained in Section <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Training details ‣ Appendix C Experiment details ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>. We initialize the variance head randomly, while we initialize the weights of the mean prediction with the weights of the last convolutional layer of the Stable Diffusion UNet.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the exact training procedure of Marigold <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ke et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. Training is done on the synthetic datasets Hypersim <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roberts et al., 2021</a>]</cite> and VKitti2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cabon et al., 2020</a>]</cite>. We use the same affine-invariant depth normalization and annealed multi-resolution noise as Marigold during training, while using Gaussian noise during inference. We perform 1000 diffusion steps with the DDPM scheduler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>]</cite>. We train using an effective batch size of 32 with Adam <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2017</a>]</cite> and convergence takes about 3 days on a single Nvidia RTX GPU. We train all models with the same setup and also retrain Marigold (<math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\delta}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜹</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\delta}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation datasets</h4>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The evaluation is performed on five real-world datasets. NYUv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib57" title="" class="ltx_ref">Silberman et al., 2012</a>]</cite> and ScanNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2017</a>]</cite> are both indoor scene datasets captured with an RGB-D Kinect sensor. NYUv2 has a designated test split with 654 images, which we use. For ScenNet, we sample 800 images from the 312 official validation scenes for testing. The street-scene dataset KITTI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geiger et al., 2012</a>]</cite> comes with a sparse metric depth captured by a LiDAR sensor and we use the Eigen test split <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Eigen et al., 2014</a>]</cite> made of 652 images. ETH3D <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schops et al., 2017</a>]</cite> and DIODE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vasiljevic et al., 2019</a>]</cite> are high-resolution datasets. We utilize the entire ETH3D dataset and the entire validation split of DIODE, which comprises 325 indoor and 446 outdoor samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation details</h4>

<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math> denoising steps and an ensemble size of <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=10</annotation></semantics></math> for every method. Marigold is tackling affine-invariant depth estimation and thus, the predictions have to be transformed before the evaluation. Furthermore, Marigold proposed to use an ensemble prediction to boost the performance and aligned the sample predictions <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{\hat{d}^{1}},...,\bm{\hat{d}^{N}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>𝟏</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝑵</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{\hat{d}^{1}},...,\bm{\hat{d}^{N}}\}</annotation></semantics></math> among each other by minimizing the following objective:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}s_{1},\ldots,s_{N}\\
t_{1},\ldots,t_{N}\end{subarray}}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1}{b}\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=i+1}^{N}\|\bm{\hat{d}^{i^{\prime}}}-\bm{\hat{d}^{j^{\prime}}}\|_{2}^{2}}+\lambda\mathcal{R}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>𝒊</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">′</mo></msup></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>𝒋</mi><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}s_{1},\ldots,s_{N}\\
t_{1},\ldots,t_{N}\end{subarray}}\left(\sqrt{\frac{1}{b}\sum_{i=1}^{N-1}\sum_{j=i+1}^{N}\|\bm{\hat{d}^{i^{\prime}}}-\bm{\hat{d}^{j^{\prime}}}\|_{2}^{2}}+\lambda\mathcal{R}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{d}}^{i^{\prime}}=\hat{s}^{i}\bm{\hat{d}}^{i}+\hat{t}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>t</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{d}}^{i^{\prime}}=\hat{s}^{i}\bm{\hat{d}}^{i}+\hat{t}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the scaled and shifted predictions, <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}=|\min(m)|+|1-\max(m)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=|\min(m)|+|1-\max(m)|</annotation></semantics></math> is a regularization term with <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}(x,y)=\text{median}(\bm{\hat{d}}^{1^{\prime}}(x,y),...,\bm{\hat{d}}^{N^{\prime}}(x,y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒎</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>median</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}(x,y)=\text{median}(\bm{\hat{d}}^{1^{\prime}}(x,y),...,\bm{\hat{d}}^{N^{\prime}}(x,y))</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\binom{N}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>N</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\binom{N}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is a hyperparameter. Then, the median <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒎</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken and aligned with the target depth map by a least squares fit <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}=s\bm{m}+t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒎</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}=s\bm{m}+t</annotation></semantics></math>. We follow Marigold and perform the same steps for every method to get the point prediction <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒂</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}</annotation></semantics></math>. As we are also interested in metrics that consider the whole ensemble, such as ES and CRPS, further align the ensemble by setting <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}^{i}=s\bm{\hat{d}}^{i^{\prime}}+t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}^{i}=s\bm{\hat{d}}^{i^{\prime}}+t</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., we align each ensemble member with the same transformation that we computed for the median <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{d}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We evaluate the prediction using the UQ metrics ES and CRPS and the metrics reported in Marigold (<math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{d}=(d_{i})_{i=1,...,M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒅</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{d}=(d_{i})_{i=1,...,M}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the true depth map and <math id="A3.SS5.SSS0.Px4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> the number of pixels):</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Absolute Mean Relativ Error (<span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AbsRel</span>): <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{M}\Sigma_{i=1}^{M}|a_{i}-d_{i}|/d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{M}\Sigma_{i=1}^{M}|a_{i}-d_{i}|/d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> Accuracy: Proportion of pixels satisfying <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(a_{i}/d_{i},d_{i}/a_{i})&lt;1.25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1.25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(a_{i}/d_{i},d_{i}/a_{i})&lt;1.25</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Additional results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides more detailed results of the different experiments.
Tables <a href="#A4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, <a href="#A4.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#A4.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> outline several considered metrics for the UCI dataset with standard deviations.
Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows the results for the different autoregressive prediction tasks, averaged over five runs (except for T2M). While we report the average time per training epoch, the underlying algorithms are not optimized and might heavily depend on the used architecture and the availability of the compute cluster. They should therefore only be seen as a rough estimate for identifying methods that take a significantly longer time for training. Corresponding visualizations of the different methods can be found in Figures <a href="#A4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
Table <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ Appendix D Additional results ‣ Improved probabilistic regression usingdiffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows more results of the depth estimation task.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T5" class="ltx_table">
