<figure id="A7.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span>Effect of the covariance matrix approximation and the kernel bandwidth <math id="A7.T13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> on the performance on the validation set. The numerical values for <math id="A7.T13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> denote the rank in the low-rank approximation, while C denotes the full Cholesky approximation. For the KS data, training with <math id="A7.T13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=5</annotation></semantics></math> did not converge. For readability, the metrics RMSE, ES, and CRPS are scaled by the factor 100 (10) for the Burgers’ (KS) data.</figcaption>
